# pnpm settings live in pnpm-workspace.yaml (pnpm 11 no longer reads them
# from .npmrc, and the two that used to live here — auto-install-peers=true,
# strict-peer-dependencies=false — are pnpm defaults anyway).

# IMPORTANT: No auth tokens in this file!
# npm publish authentication is handled via:
#   - CI: trusted publishing (OIDC) from the publish-packages.yml workflow.
#         No token is involved -- there is no NPM_TOKEN secret.
#   - Local (break-glass, i.e. a new package's first version): a granular access
#         token with "Bypass 2FA" in the USER-LEVEL ~/.npmrc, publish without
#         --provenance, delete the token afterwards. Packages that already exist
#         disallow tokens, so unattended local publishing is not possible — writes
#         to them (npm deprecate, re-publish) need `npm login --auth-type=web`.
#         Full steps in the root CLAUDE.md, "Publishing Libraries to npm".
